**`pup land` refuses every PR when the origin remote's case differs from GitHub's.**

```ts
const prefix = `https://${repo}/pull/`;
if (!prUrl.startsWith(prefix) || !/^\d+$/.test(prUrl.slice(prefix.length))) {
```

`repo` comes from `originRepoSlug(recorded origin url)`, which never lowercases (github.client.ts L31-L37). For example, `git@github.com:alexisbalayre/pupitre.git` gives `github.com/alexisbalayre/pupitre`. `prUrl` is the stdout of `gh pr create`, or the `url` from `gh pr list`, and GitHub renders both in the repo's canonical case (`https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/pull/12`).

The merge path only passes the slug to gh as `--repo`, and GitHub resolves that without regard to case, so `pup merge --pr` succeeds. This new `startsWith` is the only place the two are compared as text. Re-running `pup land` gives the same refusal every time. The only way out is to repoint origin to the canonical case and run `pup init --origin-moved`.

**Suggested fix:** compare the prefix case-insensitively. Restrict the comparison to ASCII so a character such as U+212A cannot fold into a match. Two names that differ only by case are the same GitHub repo, so the protection against another repo's PR is kept.

```ts
const head = prUrl.slice(0, prefix.length);
if (
  !/^[!-~]+$/.test(head) ||
  head.toLowerCase() !== prefix.toLowerCase() ||
  !/^\d+$/.test(prUrl.slice(prefix.length))
) {
```

*(GitHub's url casing is pinned-version knowledge, hence medium confidence.)*

